An additional genus was placed in this family but later determined to be a taphonomic variant (2006-00-00-p Long stalked eocrinoids in the basal Middle Cambrian Kaili Biota, Taijiang County, Guizhou Province, China.pdf)
==Description==
''Lichenoides'' is stemless<ref name=Zamora2017>{{harvnb|Zamora|Deline|Javier Álvaro|Rahman|2017}}</ref>, being one of a "handful" of eocrinoid taxa where the stem is absent or reduced.

==Phylogeny==
''Lichenoides'' is the sole formally described genus in the family Lichenoididae (sometimes misspelled Lichenoidae), although a second genus has been identified but not yet described.<ref name=Smith2013>{{harvnb|Smith|Zamora|Javier Álvaro|2013}}</ref>  Lichenoididae is crownwards from the [[Gogiida]] but basal to all other eocrinoides and other blastozoans that are more derived than gogiids as shown in the following cladogram, after Nardin et al. 2017 with slight modifications:<ref name=Nardin2017>{{harvnb|Nardin|Lefebvre|Fatka|Nohejlová|Kašička|Šinágl|Szabad|2017}}</ref>

